The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app
targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,
misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real,
compiled canonical feature-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/**` — where every
sibling P7 page ships (Admin/*, Exports, Explore, Maps, Dashboard, …) and which `Sources`
already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Settings`. Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/
Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same reconciliation every sibling
page log records (AuditLog, DiskForecast, SchemaDrift, …); it is the only deviation from
the literal prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the settings sub-path `/settings/safety`. Following the
sibling nested-route pattern (`.notificationsAudit` pathSegment "notifications/audit" +
alias; `.auditLog` + alias), a dedicated `.settingsSafety` AppRoute case is added
(pathSegment `settings/safety`, Account group, icon `exclamationmark.shield.fill`),
`AppRouteParser` aliases `/settings/safety` → `.settingsSafety`, and
`SafetyRouteRegistration` hosts `SafetyPage` on it, chained into `\.routeHosts` in
TeslaSyncApp.swift beside `SettingsRouteRegistration`. So the page is reachable via the
Account-group sidebar entry and any `/settings/safety` deep link, without displacing the
main `.settings` page. Only AppRoute.swift's three exhaustive AppRoute switches
(pathSegment / systemImage / group) needed the new case — verified the only `case .dashboard`
switches in the app target are AppRoute.swift's; ExploreCatalog.gating has a `default`;
WatchDeepLink is a separate enum. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

AI EXPLAINER SCOPE: the web page also renders the opt-in `<AISafetySettingExplainer>` ABOVE
this panel, but ONLY when that feature is enabled — ADR-015 §I5 hidden UI: in the default /
AI-OFF state it is absent from the DOM. The manifest scopes THIS parity unit to the listing
panel (`GlassPanel1`) only; the explainer is its own separately-tracked Apple surface
(apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISafetySettingExplainer.*). The faithful default
render of the web page (feature off) is exactly this listing — which is what ships here.

